James inquired about whether to report damage to his car, which was struck while parked, and how it might affect his insurance premiums. I advised him to consider the repair costs relative to his $500 deductible and the potential impact on his premiums. After James confirmed the estimated damage was likely under his deductible, I suggested obtaining quotes from local repair shops to assess costs before making a claim. I also reassured him that he could wait to file a claim until after receiving a quote, while emphasizing the importance of adhering to his insurer's reporting timeframe and gathering documentation. This informed him on how to proceed effectively with his situation.
